# Scripts are checked out with LF on every platform.
#
# `scripts/public-export.mjs` is imported by its test, not merely executed, and
# a module checked out with CRLF fails to parse if it opens with a shebang —
# CI on windows-latest reported "SyntaxError: Invalid or unexpected token"
# while every LF checkout passed. That shebang is gone, but pinning the
# endings removes the whole class rather than the one instance.
scripts/*.mjs text eol=lf
scripts/*.js  text eol=lf
